<.shell title="Build a group rule" current={:build_a_group_rule}>
  <h1>Build a group rule</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    An editor inside a page: small inputs and small buttons, since it sits among other content.
  </p>

  <div class="example measure">
    <.clause_editor clauses={clauses()} />
  </div>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Each clause is a <a href={page_path(:card)}>card</a>
      with a name and the qualifications a member must hold any of.
    </li>
    <li>
      Each qualification is a chip with a button that removes it. A qualification D4H no longer
      has is a red chip, so it's easy to find and remove.
    </li>
    <li>Done closes the editor. Members change only after you review and send the changes.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="spec">
    <code>&lt;.clause_editor clauses=&#123;…&#125; /&gt;</code>
    from <code>Web.Components.GroupRule</code>, as on a group's page, with made-up clauses.
  </p>
</.shell>
